ignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nfour point five stable\n\n### System information\n\nn/a\n\n### Issue description\n\nusing custom gltf data, and a `GLTFDocumentExtension`, \n\nI am able to edit and process the incoming glTF scene. However, when it comes to the editor and the animations in the AnimationPlayer of the scene, I am unable to make it play automatically. \n\nWith `Animation.current_animation` being a special editor only property that is not meant to be edited, I am unable to get the godot editor to autoplay an animation I choose when i add the gltf to my scene, **in the editor.**\n\nSimply, I want to import a glTF scene in editor, and have one of its animations play automatically, always, when i drag it into the Scene tab. \n\nFor example, if I drag in a \"Spinning Box\" asset to the Scene tab, I would have something in the glTF to say that the \"Spinning\" animation is the default and to play this when the player is `ready`. \n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nIt is kind of complicated but the steps are:\n\n1. make a GLTFDocumentExtension script and register it in a plugin\n2. in the script, select an animation and set the `AnimationPlayer.current_animation` to your desired action.\n3. on import, the property is empty, meaning the animation doesn't automatically play and the code doesn't really work.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nn/a","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":